IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-cantonal`

-- bgg4-tests-cantonal: tests for Art 110 to 112.  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Art 110 tests`

-- "Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben, gewährleisten sie, dass dieses selbst oder eine vorgängig zuständige andere richterliche Behörde den Sachverhalt frei prüft und das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet."
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 111 tests`

-- (1) "Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können."
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the canton has let the person take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the canton has let the person take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the canton has let the person take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Bundesbehörden, die zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt sind, können die Rechtsmittel des kantonalen Rechts ergreifen und sich vor jeder kantonalen Instanz am Verfahren beteiligen, wenn sie dies beantragen."
#ASSERT `Art 111(2) the federal authority may take the remedies of cantonal law and take part before every cantonal instance` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(2) the federal authority may take the remedies of cantonal law and take part before every cantonal instance` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 111(2) the federal authority may take the remedies of cantonal law and take part before every cantonal instance` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "Die unmittelbare Vorinstanz des Bundesgerichts muss mindestens die Rügen nach den Artikeln 95–98 prüfen können."
#ASSERT `Art 111(3) the immediate lower instance can examine at least the complaints under Art 95 to 98` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(3) the immediate lower instance can examine at least the complaints under Art 95 to 98` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 112 tests`

-- (1) "Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen."
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision is notified to the parties in writing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision is notified to the parties in writing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision is notified to the parties in writing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(a) "die Begehren, die Begründung, die Beweisvorbringen und Prozesserklärungen der Parteien, soweit sie nicht aus den Akten hervorgehen": order is subject to appeal, contains, appear from the files
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(b) "die massgebenden Gründe tatsächlicher und rechtlicher Art, insbesondere die Angabe der angewendeten Gesetzesbestimmungen"
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(b) the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(b) the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(b) the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(c) "das Dispositiv"
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(c) the decision contains the operative part` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(c) the decision contains the operative part` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(c) the decision contains the operative part` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(d) "eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht": order is subject to appeal, notice, value limit, states value
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) the paragraph: subject, written, (a) contains, (a) from files, (b), (c), notice, value limit, states value
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) first sentence
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the authority may notify the decision promptly and without reasons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the authority may notify the decision promptly and without reasons` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) second sentence: "Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen."  Notified 1 March 2026: the 30th day after is 31 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the last day to demand the complete version` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the last day to demand the complete version` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 EQUALS JUST (Date 7 4 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the last day to demand the complete version` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 (Date 7 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 (Date 8 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) third sentence: order is notified without reasons, day notified, days left out, demanded within the period, complete version notified, day asked about
-- the bar applies while the period runs and no complete version has come
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the last day itself: the period has not run out yet
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the day after: the period ran out unused, the bar is lifted
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a demand was made and the complete version has not come: the bar applies even after the 30 days
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 TRUE FALSE (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a demand was made and the complete version was notified: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 TRUE TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the complete version was notified before the 30 days ran out
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- days left out of the count move the day the period runs out
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 FALSE FALSE (Date 7 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) 7 FALSE FALSE (Date 8 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a decision notified without reasons: the sentence does not reach it
#ASSERT `Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) 0 FALSE FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "Das Bundesgericht kann einen Entscheid, der den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt, an die kantonale Behörde zur Verbesserung zurückweisen oder aufheben."
#ASSERT `Art 112(3) the Court may remit the decision for improvement or quash it` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(3) the Court may remit the decision for improvement or quash it` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "Für die Gebiete, in denen Bundesbehörden zur Beschwerde berechtigt sind, bestimmt der Bundesrat, welche Entscheide ihnen die kantonalen Behörden zu eröffnen haben."
#ASSERT `Art 112(4) the cantonal authority must notify the decision to the federal authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(4) the cantonal authority must notify the decision to the federal authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(4) the cantonal authority must notify the decision to the federal authority` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The duties as regulative rules: traces (printed, not asserted)`

-- Art 110, 111(1), 111(3): the cantons' duties have no time limit; with the act done the duty is fulfilled, with nothing done it stands
#TRACE `Art 110 the cantons' duty to ensure the review by a judicial authority` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `ensure that the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts and applies the law of its own motion` AT 5
#TRACE `Art 111(1) the cantons' duty to let a person entitled to appeal take part as a party` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `let a person entitled to appeal take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` AT 5
#TRACE `Art 111(3) the cantons' duty to let the immediate lower instance examine the complaints under Art 95 to 98` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Canton DOES `let the immediate lower instance examine at least the complaints under Art 95 to 98` AT 5
-- Art 112(1): the cantonal authority's duty to notify in writing
#TRACE `Art 112(1) the cantonal authority's duty to notify the decision to the parties in writing` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Lower instance` DOES `notify the decision to the parties in writing` AT 2
-- Art 112(2): the parties' 30 days to demand the complete version; the demand on day 30 and on day 31
#TRACE `Art 112(2) the parties' permission to demand the complete version within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Party to the proceedings` DOES `demand the complete version of the decision` AT 30
#TRACE `Art 112(2) the parties' permission to demand the complete version within 30 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Party to the proceedings` DOES `demand the complete version of the decision` AT 31
